jobs.description:
A leading global investment firm is looking for an experienced Equity Research Analyst
to join its investment team in Hong Kong.

The role will focus on Hardware, Industrials and Financials
, with an investment universe spanning China A-shares, Hong Kong, the US, Japan and Korea
. The investment approach combines top-down and bottom-up research
, integrating macroeconomic trends, policy developments, industry cycles and global supply-chain dynamics with in-depth company fundamental analysis.

The ideal candidate will have strong fundamental research capabilities, prior buy-side experience
, meaningful exposure to the China onshore market
, and the ability to translate research into actionable investment views.

Responsibilities
Conduct in-depth fundamental research across Hardware, Industrials and Financials
in China, Hong Kong, the US, Japan and Korea;
Develop top-down views based on macro trends, policy developments, industry cycles, capex, supply-demand dynamics and global supply chains;
Conduct bottom-up company research covering business models, competitive positioning, earnings drivers and valuation;
Build and maintain financial models, earnings forecasts and valuation frameworks;
Conduct primary research through management meetings, industry experts, suppliers, customers and other industry participants;
Identify expectation gaps, fundamental inflection points and potential catalysts;
Support the Portfolio Manager while also independently generating Long / Short investment ideas and forming investment views within assigned coverage
;
Clearly articulate investment thesis, upside/downside, catalysts and key risks;
Continuously monitor portfolio holdings and key research names as macro, industry and company fundamentals evolve.

Requirements
Approximately 5–8 years of equity research or investment experience
;
Prior buy-side experience
from a leading hedge fund, mutual fund, asset manager or other institutional investment platform;
Strong experience in the China onshore market
, combined with a global equity investment perspective;
Deep sector expertise in at least one of the following:
Hardware / Technology Hardware:
electronics, semiconductors, consumer electronics, components and related supply chains;
Industrials:
manufacturing, industrial automation, machinery and capital goods;
Financials:
banks, insurance, brokers and diversified financials;
Strong ability to combine top-down and bottom-up investment frameworks
;
Excellent fundamental research, financial modelling and valuation skills;
Ability to develop independent investment views rather than simply follow market consensus;
Strong analytical ability, commercial judgment and intellectual curiosity;
Degree from a leading university;
Fluent Mandarin and strong professional English.

